="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/thor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Thor</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Thor was the Germanic god of thunder, known to the continental Saxons as Thunaer or Donar and to the English as Thunor.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/thorfinn-the-mighty"><span class="enc-name">Thorfinn the Mighty</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Thorfinn the Mighty (c. 1009–c. 1065) was Earl of Orkney and a grandson, through his mother, of the Scottish king Malcolm II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/thorigny-marble"><span class="enc-name">Thorigny Marble</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Thorigny Marble is an inscribed Roman statue base of 238 CE, found at Vieux, ancient Aregenua, in Normandy and now kept at Saint-Lô.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/thorn-netherlands"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/thorn-netherlands.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Thorn, Netherlands</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Thorn is a small town in the province of Limburg in the south-eastern Netherlands, near the Meuse.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/thoros-i-prince-of-armenia"><span class="enc-name">Thoros I, Prince of Armenia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Thoros I was the Rubenid lord of Armenian Cilicia from about 1100 to 1129.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/thoros-ii-prince-of-armenia"><span class="enc-name">Thoros II, Prince of Armenia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Thoros II was the Rubenid lord of Armenian Cilicia from about 1144 to 1169.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/thoros-of-ed